    "tokenizer_n_vocab": 248320,
    "true_ternary": true,
    "save_dir": "/dev/shm/pithagoras-moe-checkpoints",
    "ternary_model_dir": "/dev/shm/pithagoras-moe-checkpoints/model-30b/ternary-30b-files",
    "ternary_model_format": "native ternary per-layer/per-expert files",
    "n_layers": 64,
    "n_embd": 5120,
    "n_ffn": 17408,
    "n_head": 24,
    "n_head_kv": 4,
    "n_vocab": 248320,
    "dtype": "ternary {-1,0,+1} (2-bit packed)",
    "model_desc": "27B qwen35 MoE (Bonsai-27B) ternary export -> ~30B, kept in the teacher 27B MoE token space (n_vocab 248320)",
    "compressed_token_input": false,
    "chunk_size": 4,
    "chunk_token_offset": 0,
    "compressed_token_input_note": "Set true (or env COMPRESSED_INPUT=1) to feed the model CHUNKED/compressed tokens (chunk_id = vocab_offset + floor(rawId/chunk_size)) instead of raw ids; the compressed-token scoring (footprint = sum of ids) always runs."
  },
  "etokens": {
    "enabled": true,
    "build_base": true,
    "live_update": true,
    "chunk_size": 4,
    "file": "data/Etokens.json",
    "train_scope": "new_3b_only",
    "note": "E-TOKEN COMPRESSION SYSTEM (corrected): data/Etokens.json stores recallable functions etoken(e1) -> (o1,o2,o3,o2,o4) (the original token tuple, deduped of effective adjacent repeats). On startup the pre-tokenized token DB (data/project-tokens.json) is fed through the e-tokenizer to BUILD the base Etokens.json; then every teacher-generated chunk is e-tokenized and MERGED back live (etokens.live_update). The etoken id (in moe.new_token_base..+new_token_count) is the deterministic/recallable handle in the reserved range. TRAIN SCOPE (user directive): we are ONLY training the NEW ~3B parameters (the 30B-27B delta: mutation / mtp_head / new_token / compr* experts \u2014 isNewNetwork in teacher-live.mjs) to use the new etokens and produce COMPRESSED (etoken) output. Base 27B experts E1..E5 are NOT trained for etoken emission. Later we move to the model as a whole using this 3B 'expert' to save space/memory. ATM we train the final 3B expert/set to give compressed token output: etoken disqualification + repeat-train-top-k + phase-1 compressed-output reward apply ONLY to new-3B networks. An expert that produces a token whose ORIGINAL token is NOT in the teacher's top-k is DISQUALIFIED (no reward) for the round, and the etoken id is repeat-trained into each new expert's top-k until it appears (etokens.mjs).",
    "disqualify_round": true,
    "repeat_train_topk_max_passes": 40
  },
  "moe": {
    "num_experts": 50,
    "always_active": 50,
    "topk_route": 6,
    "mtp_trained": true,
    "mtp_expert": "EMTP",
    "compressor_tokens_only": true,
    "allow_new_token_output": true,
    "expert_steering": 0.3,
    "steering_max_bias": 2,
    "steering_top_n": 20,
    "skip_teacher_when_poor": true,
    "poor_topk_threshold": 0.1,
    "self_update_when_poor": true,
    "new_token_base": 200000,
    "new_token_count": 512,
    "create_new_token_experts": true,
    "new_token_formula_note": "USER CORRECTION: the compressed token must be a GENUINELY NEW token (a reserved id in [new_token_base, new_token_base+new_token_count)), NOT sum%n_vocab folded onto an existing vocab token. Its VALUE = the sum of the constituent token ids (footprint); its reserved id = new_token_base + (rawSum % new_token_count) \u2014 deterministic and decompressible (the rawSum is recoverable). create_new_token_experts=true makes the harness ADD a new MoE expert per distinct new token (NT<idx>) so each new token has its own network that learns to emit it, then steering/logit-bias 'convinces' the model to use that new token.",
    "compressor_role": "mutations",
    "compressor_note": "EACH COMPRESSOR MUST USE ONLY COMPRESSOR TOKENS: experts designated as compressors (role starts with 'compr' or listed in compressor_experts) may only route/emit tokens from the compressor-token set (the compressed-chunk / formulaic tokens in newTokenSet), never the general vocabulary. This is what makes the extra layers fight to become token-COMPRESSOR layers (they can only express compressed tokens). allow_new_token_output=true lets those compressor experts actually EMIT the compressed new token as part of the scored output (so 500x can fire), instead of only matching it one-directionally. skip_teacher_when_poor / self_update_when_poor: when the student top-k is BAD (best overlap < poor_topk_threshold), DON'T spend resources having the teacher generate a fresh top-k \u2014 reuse the existing reference and just update the COMPRESSION experts from the student's own generation output instead.",
    "compressor_experts": [
      "EMTP",
      "E101",
      "E100",
      "E99"
    ],
    "expert_structure": {
      "n_segments_3b": 3,
      "n_experts_per_segment": 25,
      "attach_best_only": true,
      "layers_per_expert": 4,
      "rewire_every": 10,
      "rewire_rate": 0.05,
      "note": "GRANULAR 3B STRUCTURE (user-corrected): MULTIPLE 3B segments trained in parallel (n_segments_3b=3), only the BEST is attached. We do NOT preset neurons/expert \u2014 sizes SEED small and EVOLVE via rewiring. REWIRING IS RANK-SCALED (user): the attached BEST segment NEVER changes ('best contains no change ever'); LOSERS mutate by rank 'layer change for less performing models increases based on position': loser at 1-based rank `place` changes (place-1)*5% of its neurons (floor 0 at the top loser, worst loser mutates most aggressively). rewire_every=steps between rewires; rewire_rate=base fraction (per-place step is +5%)."
    },
