    "curve": {
      "enabled": true,
      "exp_base": 2,
      "exp_scaler": 4,
      "note": "exponential reward for matching the (perfect) teacher's top-k curve: each matched teacher slot i pays per_topk_token_match * exp_base^((i+1)/exp_scaler), so MORE matches = MORE reward (progressively). A compressed token that lands on a teacher slot counts and is multiplied by compressed_token_mult. New-token-system tokens in the teacher top-k are also heavily rewarded.",
      "compressed_token_mult": 4,
      "degenerate_freezes_reward": true
    },
    "compression": {
      "enabled": true,
      "base_effective_tokens": 5,
      "reference_tokens": 23,
      "text_length_factor": 1,
      "multiplier": 1,
      "new_token_match_mult": 1.001,
      "new_token_match_min_pct": 0.2,
      "tally_before_reset": true,
      "degenerate_penalty": -50,
      "degenerate_partial": false,
      "note": "compression_reward = compressionRatio * baseEffectiveTokens * ( 1 + textLengthGenerated / tokensSaved ) ; \ncompressionRatio = referenceTokens / emittedTokens ; tokensSaved = referenceTokens - emittedTokens. If >=min_pct of generated tokens match new-token-system created tokens, multiply by new_token_match_mult * tokensSaved. DEGENERATE GUARD: if the student emits ALL the same token (a repeated-token attractor like '/'), the compression reward is frozen to 0 (degenerate_partial=false) and degenerate_penalty is applied, so a collapsed student can't farm points for trivially repeating one token."
    },
    "two_phase": {
      "enabled": true,
      "phase": 1,
      "new_net_compression_weight": 40,
      "reconstruct_weight": 120,
      "reconstruct_top_k": 20,
      "reconstruct_min_overlap": 0.5,
      "note": "USER DESIGN: (PHASE 1) the NEW networks (all mutation + MTP experts beyond the 5 base ones) are trained to FAVOR compressed tokens \u2014 each new network that emits a compressed/new token (in newTokenSet) earns new_net_compression_weight per position, so the added networks become token-COMPRESSORS. (PHASE 2) the new compressed experts must then reproduce the SAME SHAPE as if they weren't attached: when a new network is active, its position's top-k must match the BASE (un-attached, E1-E5) experts' top-k at that position (reconstruct_min_overlap) \u2014 scoring reconstruct_weight times the base-overlap. Setting phase=2 gates reconstruction scoring on; phase=1 gates the compression-favor on. Both reward only NEW networks (role mutation/mtp_head), never the base experts."
    },
    "compare": {
      "mode": "topk_first",
      "identical_settings": false,
      "top_k": 20,
      "top_p": 0.95,
      "temperature": 0.7,
      "note": "USER DIRECTIVE + ROOT-CAUSE FIX: analyse the teacher/student top-k head-to-head. identical_settings=false (CHANGED 2026-08-16) so the TEACHER uses top_k/top_p/temperature above (cold, coherent) while the STUDENT uses its OWN emit settings (sampling.emit.student: temperature 2.0, top_k 100, top_p 0.99) \u2014 the TQ1_0 student verifiably COLLAPSES to a single repeated token ('apart') at cold temp 0.7, flattening the score graph. Hot student sampling breaks the collapse so its top-k can overlap the teacher's coherent top-k. Both now generate a real multi-token chunk (compareN=STUDENT_STEP) instead of a single top-1 token."
    }
